            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "Saurav-Gupta-9741"
            },
            "body": "Hi @njhill Sir, @benchislett Sir, @LucasWilkinson Sir, and @luccafong Sir,\r\n\r\nI hope you are all having a great week!\r\n\r\nJust wanted to give a quick update on this PR:\r\n1. I have **rebased onto latest `upstream/main`**, resolving all merge conflicts in `vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/autoregressive/speculator.py`.\r\n2. Cleaned up code formatting to be **100% `ruff` compliant**.\r\n3. Squashed into **1 single clean commit** (`9928029d0`) with full DCO sign-off (`DCO -> success` ✅).\r\n\r\nThe PR fixes the CUDA illegal memory access issue during speculator CUDA graph capture on H100s by zeroing draft speculation state buffers before capture.\r\n\r\nCould one of you please add the `ready` label to authorize the self-hosted GPU runner CI to run?\r\n\r\nThank you so much for your time and guidance!\r\n\r\nLooking Forward for the Response",
